Subject: [PATCH] media: qcom: iris: expose gen1 encoder repeat headers

Korri-local patch against Linux 7.2. SM8250 uses the gen1 HFI boolean
HFI_PROPERTY_CONFIG_VENC_SYNC_FRAME_SEQUENCE_HEADER, not the gen2 header
mode enum. Expose PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR and consume it when HEADER_MODE
programs that boolean, as gen2 already consumes this companion control.
Both controls remain static (set before streaming).

The Qualcomm SM8250 Venus driver maps PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR directly to
this property with struct hfi_enable: msm_venc_set_sequence_header_mode()
in techpack/video/msm/vidc/msm_venc.c, lines 3504-3536, at
LineageOS/android_kernel_xiaomi_sm8250 commit
f3d39dae3253e7f8bb623eb83a146088f3174148. Thus it is the repeat-at-IDR switch,
not a distinct first-frame-only switch. Linux 7.2 Venus venc.c:876-888
already enables it for HEADER_MODE_JOINED_WITH_1ST_FRAME, as does Iris.

Preserve that existing HEADER_MODE mapping when prepend is disabled;
enabling prepend overrides separate mode. Gen1 has only this one boolean:
joined mode therefore still enables repeating headers even when prepend
is zero. This patch does not invent independently selectable gen2 modes.
Actual firmware output must still be checked for SPS/PPS before later IDRs.

Pair with the existing upstream add-request-key-frame-support patch for
FORCE_KEY_FRAME. Gen1 already reads picture_type from the compressed FBD
packet and maps IDR/I to KEYFRAME; no gen2 subscription patch is needed.

--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_hfi_gen1.c
@@ -127,6 +127,13 @@
 		.flags = CAP_FLAG_OUTPUT_PORT | CAP_FLAG_MENU,
 		.set = iris_set_header_mode_gen1,
 	},
+	{
+		.cap_id = PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR,
+		.min = 0,
+		.max = 1,
+		.step_or_mask = 1,
+		.value = 0,
+	},
 	{
 		.cap_id = BITRATE,
 		.min = BITRATE_MIN,
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_ctrls.c
@@ -605,11 +605,17 @@
 int iris_set_header_mode_gen1(struct iris_inst *inst, enum platform_inst_fw_cap_type cap_id)
 {
 	const struct iris_hfi_session_ops *hfi_ops = inst->hfi_session_ops;
+	u32 prepend_sps_pps = inst->fw_caps[PREPEND_SPSPPS_TO_IDR].value;
 	u32 header_mode = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].value;
 	u32 hfi_id = inst->fw_caps[cap_id].hfi_id;
 	u32 hfi_val;
 
-	if (header_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE)
+	/*
+	 * Gen1 prefixes sync frames with sequence headers using one boolean.
+	 * Keep the existing joined-header behavior when prepend is disabled.
+	 */
+	if (!prepend_sps_pps &&
+	    header_mode == V4L2_MPEG_VIDEO_HEADER_MODE_SEPARATE)
 		hfi_val = 0;
 	else
 		hfi_val = 1;
